## TextareaControl props

| Prop | Type | Required | Default |
|---|---|---|---|
| `help` | `string \| Element` | No | Not stated |
| `hideLabelFromVision` | `boolean` | No | Not stated |
| `label` | `string` | No | Not stated |
| `onChange` | `(value: string) => void` | Yes | None |
| `rows` | `number` | No | `4` |
| `value` | `string` | Yes | None |

- **help**: When set, generates help text from this content.
- **hideLabelFromVision**: When `true`, the label is visible only to screen readers.
- **label**: When set, generates a label from this content.
- **onChange**: Receives the new textarea value on each change.
- **rows**: The number of rows the textarea contains.
- **value**: The current textarea value.

Props not in this list are applied to the underlying textarea element.

## Usage example

```jsx
import { useState } from 'react';
import { TextareaControl } from '@wordpress/components';

const MyTextareaControl = () => {
    const [ text, setText ] = useState( '' );

    return (
        <TextareaControl
            label="Text"
            help="Enter some text"
            value={ text }
            onChange={ ( value ) => setText( value ) }
        />
    );
};
```

## Notes

- The page does not mention `__nextHasNoMarginBottom` or any deprecation notice, so I can't confirm either from this content.
- For single-line input, the page recommends `TextControl` instead.

